### Note: This file is used to test and validate the Book Management Endpoints.
### It aligns perfectly with the BooksController using MediatR and Fluent Results.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5165/api
@contentType = application/json

### 1. Get Paginated Books List
### Retrieves a filtered, sorted, and projected list of books.
GET {{baseUrl}}/Books/books?PageNumber=1&PageSize=10
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2. Create a New Book
### Handles business logic for creating a book, attaching authors, and auto-generating copies.
POST {{baseUrl}}/Books
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Clean Architecture in C#",
  "isbn": "978-3-16-148410-4",
  "publishDate": "2026-05-11T00:00:00Z",
  "genre": 11,
  "additionalDetails": "A premium guide to software architecture.",
  "bookImageUrl": "https://cloudinary.com/libraryms/clean-arch.jpg",
  "authorIds": [1],
  "initialCopiesCount": 5
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3. Get Book By ID
### Retrieves specific book details along with its assigned authors.
GET {{baseUrl}}/Books/11
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4. Update Book Details
### Updates an existing book. Ensure that the route ID matches the body ID parameter.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/Books/11
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "id": 11,
  "title": "Clean Architecture in C#",
  "isbn": "978-3-16-148410-4",
  "publishDate": "2026-05-11T00:00:00",
  "genre": 11,
  "additionalDetails": "An updated premium guide to software architecture Asp.net.",
  "bookImageUrl": "https://cloudinary.com/libraryms/clean-arch-updated.jpg",
  "authorIds": [1, 2]
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5. Delete Book (Soft Delete)
### Triggers a soft delete sequence. Prevents deletion if active loans exist.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/Books/10
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 6. Restore Deleted Book
### Reverts the soft delete state, making the book available in active queries again.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/Books/restore/10
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 7. Get All Copies
GET {{baseUrl}}/Books/copies?BookId=10&OnlyAvailable=true&PageNumber=1&PageSize=20
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### 8. Insert new Copy
POST {{baseUrl}}/Books/11/copies
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "initialCopiesCount": 1
}

### 9. Delete Copy
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/Books/43/delete-copy
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### 10. Update Copy status
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/Books/42/update-status
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "copyStatus": 1
}

### 11. Rstore Copy
PUT {{baseUrl}}/Books/43/restore-copy
Content-Type: {{contentType}}